From: Ankit Jain <ankit-aj.jain@broadcom.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 06:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] falco.yaml: default engine.kind to kmod

Photon's falco package is built with -DBUILD_LIBSCAP_MODERN_BPF=OFF and
-DBUILD_BPF=OFF, shipping only the kmod driver (falco.ko). Upstream
falco.yaml defaults engine.kind to modern_ebpf, which causes falco to
fail at startup with:

    Error: MODERN_BPF engine is not supported in this build

Default the shipped config to the kmod driver we actually build and
install, so falco starts out-of-the-box on Photon.
---
 falco.yaml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/falco.yaml b/falco.yaml
--- a/falco.yaml
+++ b/falco.yaml
@@ -400,7 +400,7 @@
 # buffers (higher `cpus_for_each_buffer`) can lower the memory footprint.
 #
 engine:
-  kind: modern_ebpf
+  kind: kmod
   kmod:
     buf_size_preset: 4
     drop_failed_exit: false
